beed97967cbddc674c33ffe25c23352aaf5254b249750c031e8881ff32e"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":42301,"output_tokens":1451,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"5fe8ff638c6e19d9f9e3dfddff0a4824e833eaf4d3775ce3e7bc24e23aff95fd"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":43277,"output_tokens":2339,"requests":4}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the CODE clone's refresh lifecycle: what fetches origin/main after the initial clone, on what trigger, who owns it, and how the refresh interleaves with concurrent gate ref reads (or state explicitly that the clone is refreshed on redeploy only and why a redeploy-frozen main is acceptable).","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.28,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'clones the CODE side into /var/gerrit/site/mcp-code ... so it is a blobless clone that fetches objects on demand'","'the gates need a ref that tracks main, not a frozen one' — motivates a tracking ref but the design only performs an initial clone","ABSENCE: no step or trigger describes updating origin/main after the initial clone, nor who owns that refresh nor how it interleaves with concurrent gate reads"],"finding":"The plan specifies the code clone is created (--single-branch --branch main, blobless, backgrounded) but never specifies who refreshes it or when. The stated rationale for a real clone over shipping .git is that 'the gates need a ref that tracks main, not a frozen one' — yet a one-time clone freezes origin/main at clone time just like the image would, unless something periodically fetches. No fetch/refresh trigger, ownership, or concurrency-vs-gate-reads is defined.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f617bf24fb8c1a6d7","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix > Shape / Ordering","norm_id":"n9dd03dd9968a2434","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Days after deploy, review_plan against origin/main resolves an increasingly stale main; attestations pin an outdated snapshot while main has advanced","A refresh fetch racing a concurrent gate ref-resolution could read a partially-updated object DB if refresh is ever added without coordination"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State the refresh model — e.g. the clone is re-provisioned on each container (re)deploy so origin/main is as fresh as the deployed image, and gate reads only ever see a fully-materialized clone because provisioning completes atomically before REBAR_ROOT is honored; or add a periodic/operation-linked fetch with its concurrency story.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the auth/HTTPS precondition for the code-side clone in the Fix section: name whether it uses MCP_TICKETS_PAT or relies on the code URL answering ANONYMOUS git-upload-pack (HTTPS 200), and note that REBAR_ROOT is exported even when the PAT is blank.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Fix section: 'Re-using the tickets clone at REBAR_TRACKER_DIR is tempting since MCP_TICKETS_URL is the SAME repository' — names the URL but not its auth mode for the code clone.","The tickets store clones under a PAT; the plan does not say whether the new code clone needs one. This is load-bearing because REBAR_ROOT is exported unconditionally, so a blank-PAT deployment must still clone successfully — which only holds if the code URL answers anonymous requests.","T3 axis (c): auth/HTTPS preconditions must be stated for a clone integration."],"finding":"The plan proposes cloning the code side from the same repository URL as the tickets store but never states the auth/HTTPS precondition for that clone — specifically whether it uses the tickets credential (MCP_TICKETS_PAT) or relies on anonymous git-upload-pack access.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbd6170e7432cb157","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix section, 'Shape.' paragraph (clone into /var/gerrit/site/mcp-code)","norm_id":"n037cade8be7dbd94","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A deployment with MCP_TICKETS_PAT unset: if the code clone required the PAT it would fail, leaving REBAR_ROOT pointing at an empty directory and the gates broken exactly as before.","A reviewer/operator cannot confirm the clone will succeed without knowing the auth mode."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence in the 'Shape.' paragraph: the code clone requires NO credential because navapbc/rebar answers anonymous git-upload-pack over HTTPS; it therefore runs outside the PAT guard so a blank-PAT deployment still populates REBAR_ROOT.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["vague/subjective terms present: better, sufficient"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Note the runtime dependency the blobless clone introduces (gate ops may trigger on-demand fetches) and the expected behavior when the code remote is unreachable at gate time (timeout / degraded error).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a blobless clone that fetches objects on demand rather than materializing the history'","Absence: no mention of timeout/fallback behavior when the remote is unreachable during an on-demand fetch triggered by a gate op."],"finding":"The blobless clone (--filter=blob:none) fetches objects on demand at gate time; the plan does not address the runtime remote dependency this introduces — if the remote is unreachable when a gate op resolves origin/main, on-demand object fetch could fail.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3054699f94d3dd8a","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix / Shape paragraph","norm_id":"n4479805e9a05bd4b","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Gate op runs after deploy; blobless clone needs a blob not yet fetched; remote is slow/down; the gate op hangs or errors on fetch."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how a failed or unconverged mcp-code clone is surfaced to operators (a log line / readiness marker / metric distinct from the ref-resolution error) so the degraded state is observable and not confused with the pre-fix bug.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["'Until it converges the gates fail exactly as they do today — no worse.'","'A failed code clone therefore degrades to today's behaviour — the gates error — rather than blocking the deploy.'","Absence: no log/metric/alert described for clone success/failure/convergence, so a silent clone failure surfaces only as the identical 'cannot resolve ref' error this ticket exists to eliminate."],"finding":"The backgrounded code clone adds a new failure point whose failure mode is stated to be indistinguishable from the pre-fix broken state, with no described instrumentation (log/metric/alert) letting an operator tell a failed/unconverged clone apart from the old bug.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f56c9ae8f0fb8383b","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix / Ordering and Enforcement paragraphs","norm_id":"n55e4f1147068ab0c","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The mcp-code clone fails at deploy (network/remote error); gates keep erroring; an operator re-hits the exact symptom from this ticket and cannot tell it is a clone failure vs a regression."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a note that the provisioning step logs clone start/success/failure (mirroring the tickets clone) and that gate ops emit a distinguishable diagnostic when REBAR_ROOT exists but is not yet a resolvable clone.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_e